WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.001
"Marilla, can I go over and see Diana just for a minute?" asked Anne.

2
00:00:06.002 --> 00:00:09.785
"I don't want you going out after dark," said Marilla.

3
00:00:09.786 --> 00:00:13.741
"But she has something important to tell me," cried Anne.

4
00:00:13.742 --> 00:00:15.053
"How do you know?"

5
00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:18.231
"Because she just signaled me from her window.

6
00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:24.384
We make flashes with the candle by waving cardboard in front. It was my idea, Marilla!"

7
00:00:24.385 --> 00:00:28.244
"That doesn't surprise me, Anne," Marilla replied.

8
00:00:28.245 --> 00:00:31.760
Anne dashed over to Diana's and dashed back.

9
00:00:31.761 --> 00:00:36.125
"Oh, Marilla! You know that tomorrow is Diana's birthday?

10
00:00:36.126 --> 00:00:41.884
Well, she asked me to stay at her house, in the guest room!

11
00:00:41.885 --> 00:00:52.545
Her cousins are coming with a big sleigh, and we are all going to the Debating Club concert—if you'll let me go, that is. You will, won't you?"

12
00:00:52.546 --> 00:00:59.545
"No, you can't go. Little girls should not go to concerts at night," Marilla said.

13
00:00:59.546 --> 00:01:06.689
Anne, with tears rolling down her cheeks, went upstairs. Meanwhile Matthew slept on the sofa.

14
00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:14.570
Matthew opened his eyes and said, "Marilla, I think Anne should go to the concert." He had not been asleep.

15
00:01:14.571 --> 00:01:20.823
"Well, I don't," snorted Marilla. "Who's bringing up Anne, you or me?"

16
00:01:20.824 --> 00:01:28.622
"You are," admitted Matthew. But he kept asking, and eventually Marilla let Anne go to the concert.

17
00:01:28.623 --> 00:01:36.689
On the day of the concert, Diana did Anne's hair in the new style, and Anne tied Diana's bows in a special way.

18
00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:45.415
Anne felt a little sad when she compared her plain black dress and shapeless coat with Diana's pretty green dress and smart jacket.

19
00:01:45.416 --> 00:01:50.513
But Anne remembered she had an imagination and she could use it.

20
00:01:50.514 --> 00:01:56.216
Early in the evening, Diana's cousins arrived, and they crowded into the big sleigh.

21
00:01:56.217 --> 00:02:02.897
As they drove through the snow, there were tinkles of sleigh bells, and the night seemed magical to Anne.

22
00:02:02.898 --> 00:02:11.111
The concert was thrilling too. Only one item on the program failed to interest her—Gilbert Blythe reciting a poem.

23
00:02:11.112 --> 00:02:17.765
Anne picked up a book and read it until he finished, but Diana clapped and clapped for the performer.

24
00:02:17.766 --> 00:02:21.828
It was eleven o'clock when they got home, and the house was silent.

25
00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:25.034
Anne and Diana tiptoed into the guest room.

26
00:02:25.035 --> 00:02:29.951
"Are you ready for bed?" Anne asked. "Let's race to the bed!"

27
00:02:29.952 --> 00:02:36.951
The two girls ran and jumped on the bed in the spare room. And then . . . something moved under them.

28
00:02:36.952 --> 00:02:45.682
There was a gasp and a cry, and somebody said in a muffled voice, "Oh my goodness!"

29
00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:49.263
Anne and Diana dashed out of the room and up the stairs.

30
00:02:49.264 --> 00:02:51.861
It was cold and they were shivering.

31
00:02:51.862 --> 00:02:56.356
"Who was it? What was it?" whispered Anne.

32
00:02:56.357 --> 00:03:02.752
"Oh, Anne, it was Aunt Josephine. She'll be furious," answered Diana.

33
00:03:02.753 --> 00:03:05.289
"Who's Aunt Josephine?"

34
00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.419
"She's my father's aunt, and she lives in Charlottetown.

35
00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:18.040
She's really old—seventy—and I don't think she was ever young. She's very strict," Diana said.

36
00:03:18.041 --> 00:03:22.543
Miss Josephine Barry did not appear at breakfast the next morning.

37
00:03:22.544 --> 00:03:25.898
Mrs. Barry smiled kindly at the two girls.

38
00:03:25.899 --> 00:03:28.403
"Did you have a good time last night?

39
00:03:28.404 --> 00:03:35.551
I meant to tell you that Aunt Josephine came and stayed in the guest room, but I was so tired I fell asleep."

40
00:03:35.552 --> 00:03:38.809
Diana and Anne just smiled at each other.

41
00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:44.643
Anne went home after breakfast, and then later went to Mrs. Lynde's house on an errand.

42
00:03:44.644 --> 00:03:50.298
"So you nearly frightened Miss Barry to death last night?" said Mrs. Lynde.

43
00:03:50.299 --> 00:03:59.474
"Diana's mother is very upset. Josephine Barry came to stay for a month, but she changed her mind and is leaving tomorrow!

44
00:03:59.475 --> 00:04:07.778
And she had promised to pay for Diana's piano lessons, but now she isn't. She thinks Diana is a tomboy.

45
00:04:07.779 --> 00:04:12.790
Old Miss Barry is rich, and the Barrys want to keep on her good side.

46
00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:15.681
Anne, you should look before you leap.

47
00:04:15.682 --> 00:04:25.681
Especially into beds!" Mrs. Lynde laughed at her own joke, but Anne saw nothing to laugh at. Anne went back and saw Diana.

48
00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:31.762
"Anne, after you left, Aunt Josephine woke up and she was so angry!

49
00:04:31.763 --> 00:04:37.430
She won't stay, and I don't care, but Mother and Father do," said Diana.

50
00:04:37.431 --> 00:04:41.765
"Diana, didn't you say it was my fault?" asked Anne.

51
00:04:41.766 --> 00:04:46.093
"I'm no tattletale, Anne! It was my fault too."

52
00:04:46.094 --> 00:04:51.990
"Well, I'm going to tell Aunt Josephine myself," Anne announced.

53
00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:58.485
Diana stared. "Anne Shirley! Why . . . why, she'll eat you alive!"

54
00:04:58.486 --> 00:05:07.651
"I must, Diana. It was my fault and I've got to confess. Luckily, I've had practice at confessions."

55
00:05:07.652 --> 00:05:13.706
Aunt Josephine was knitting by the fire. "Who are you?" she demanded.

56
00:05:13.707 --> 00:05:19.501
"I'm Anne of Green Gables," said the small visitor, "and I've come to confess."

57
00:05:19.502 --> 00:05:23.127
"Confess what?" Miss Barry asked.

58
00:05:23.128 --> 00:05:27.356
"It was my idea that Diana and I jump on your bed.

59
00:05:27.357 --> 00:05:34.082
Diana is a very ladylike girl, and it's not fair to blame her," Anne said.

60
00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:37.599
"Diana jumped too," said Miss Barry.

61
00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.639
"It was just for fun," persisted Anne.

62
00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:48.626
"Diana really wants to learn the piano. If you must be angry, be angry with me.

63
00:05:48.627 --> 00:05:52.904
Mrs. Hammond and Mrs. Thomas were always angry at me.

64
00:05:52.905 --> 00:05:57.738
I am used to it, and I can endure it better than Diana."

65
00:05:57.739 --> 00:06:00.782
The old lady was not angry anymore.

66
00:06:00.783 --> 00:06:05.109
In fact, she was interested in this strange redheaded girl.

67
00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:10.886
"Two girls bounced on me in the middle of the night!" she said sternly.

68
00:06:10.887 --> 00:06:13.719
"You don't know what it was like."

69
00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:18.591
"I don't know, but I can imagine," Anne said eagerly.

70
00:06:18.592 --> 00:06:24.500
"It must have been very disturbing. Do you have any imagination, Miss Barry?

71
00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:28.708
If you do, imagine you are Diana and me . . .

72
00:06:28.709 --> 00:06:33.767
We didn't know there was anybody in the bed, and we nearly died!

73
00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:36.347
And we couldn't sleep in the guest room.

74
00:06:36.348 --> 00:06:39.695
You're probably used to staying in a guest room.

75
00:06:39.696 --> 00:06:45.331
But imagine you're a little orphan girl who's never stayed in a guest room."

76
00:06:45.332 --> 00:06:51.490
Miss Barry actually laughed. Diana, listening outside, was relieved.

77
00:06:51.491 --> 00:06:56.266
"My imagination is a little rusty," Miss Barry said.

78
00:06:56.267 --> 00:07:00.428
"But sit down and tell me about yourself."

79
00:07:00.429 --> 00:07:04.819
"I'm very sorry, but I can't," said Anne.

80
00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.726
"I would like to because you seem like an interesting lady.

81
00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:13.176
You might even be a kindred spirit, though you don't look like one.

82
00:07:13.177 --> 00:07:16.338
I must go home to Miss Marilla Cuthbert.

83
00:07:16.339 --> 00:07:19.917
She is a very kind lady who is bringing me up.

84
00:07:19.918 --> 00:07:24.433
But before I go, please say you forgive Diana and me."

85
00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:32.115
"If you come and talk to me sometimes, I will forgive you both," Miss Barry said.

86
00:07:32.116 --> 00:07:39.885
That evening Miss Barry gave Diana a silver bracelet and decided not to return to Charlottetown.

87
00:07:39.886 --> 00:07:46.164
"I'm staying in Avonlea so I can get acquainted with Anne," she said frankly.

88
00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:53.301
"She amuses me, and at my age, an amusing person is a rarity."

89
00:07:53.302 --> 00:07:59.350
Miss Barry stayed for more than a month, and she and Anne became firm friends.

90
00:07:59.351 --> 00:08:11.620
Anne confided to Marilla, "Miss Barry was a kindred spirit, after all!"

